      "lineage": {
        "description": "EM-DAT country profiles are derived from the global EM-DAT disaster database maintained by CRED, which aggregates disaster impact data from UN agencies, governmental and non-governmental sources, insurance companies, research institutes, and press agencies. For Croatia, records are filtered and aggregated by year, disaster group, type, and subtype to produce annual summary statistics including total events, total affected, total deaths, and total economic damage in both original and inflation-adjusted USD. The resulting dataset provides a historical time-series of multi-hazard disaster impacts at the national level for use in disaster risk analysis and policy.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "id": "source_1",
            "name": "EM-DAT: The Emergency Events Database",
            "type": "dataset",
            "risk_data_type": [
              "loss"
            ],
            "used_in": "loss",
            "description": "EM-DAT is a global disaster loss registry maintained by CRED (Centre for Research on the Epidemiology of Disasters) that compiles standardized records of natural hazard events including total events, affected population, deaths, and economic damage. This country profile aggregates EM-DAT records by year, disaster type, and subtype for Croatia."
          }
